<title>THAILAND: Bank of Thailand says reference rate 30.842.</title>
<headline>Bank of Thailand says reference rate 30.842.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand said on Wednesday the weighted average interbank exchange rate was 30.842 per dollar against 30.370 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The reference rate is the average rate traded the previous day. It has been announced daily by the central bank since the July 2 managed flotation of the baht.</p>
<p>The baht was quoted at 30.91/31.11 to the dollar onshore and 30.60/30.70 in offshore markets early.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
